    <string name="version_label">version %1$s</string>
    <string name="changelog_title">what\'s new</string>
    <string-array name="changelog_0_3_0">
        <item>Live clipboard: what you copy appears as tiles. Tap one to type it, pin it to keep it.</item>
        <item>New toolbar next to the suggestions: quick keyboard size and a shortcut to Settings.</item>
        <item>The Settings menu now loops: swipe past the last section and you are back at the first.</item>
        <item>Settings and the keyboard follow your phone\'s language (English, Spanish, French, German).</item>
        <item>Word Flow rebuilt: it looks at the whole dictionary and writes nothing when it is not sure.</item>
        <item>60,000 words per language, each language with its own dictionary.</item>
        <item>Autocorrect never changes a valid word, and Backspace undoes it.</item>
        <item>The 20 official Windows Phone accent colors and a flat clipboard icon.</item>
        <item>Fixed: repeated letters (ww, oo) selecting a word, and taps lost when typing with two thumbs.</item>
        <item>Back up settings and words to a file you choose, with no storage permission.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="changelog_0_2_0">
        <item>Swipe typing (Word Flow) and swipe left on Backspace to delete whole words.</item>
        <item>One-handed mode, light and dark themes, and hardware keyboard support.</item>
        <item>Skin tone picker for emoji, and import from the Android personal dictionary.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="changelog_0_1_0">
        <item>First release: flat Metro keys, Shift states, double space for a period and long press for accents.</item>
        <item>Offline dictionaries in four languages. No internet permission.</item>
    </string-array>

